The school cafeteria initially had 23 apples. They used 20 of these apples to make lunch for the students. After using 20 apples, the remaining number of apples is calculated as:

$$
23 - 20 = 3
$$

Next, the cafeteria bought 6 additional apples. Adding these to the remaining apples gives:

$$
3 + 6 = 9
$$

Thus, the total number of apples the cafeteria would have is:

$$
\boxed{9}
$$

