Number of adults = Total people - Number of kids
Number of adults = 13 - 9
Number of adults = 4

So there are 4 adults in the group. 

Now, each adult meal is $7. Since only the adults need to pay, the total cost should be the number of adults multiplied by the cost per adult meal. 

Total cost = Number of adults × Cost per adult meal
Total cost = 4 × $7
Total cost = $28

