Megan started with 71 cupcakes. Todd ate 43, so we subtract those from the total to find out how many are left for packaging. 

$$
71 - 43 = 28
$$

Now, Megan wants to make packages of 7 cupcakes each. To find the number of packages, divide the remaining cupcakes by the number per package:

$$
28 \div 7 = 4
$$

Thus, Megan can make $\boxed{4}$ packages. 

