The cafeteria initially has 96 apples. After handing out 42 apples to students, the remaining number of apples is calculated as follows:

$$
96 - 42 = 54
$$

Each pie requires 6 apples. To determine how many pies can be made, we divide the remaining apples by the number of apples per pie:

$$
54 \div 6 = 9
$$

Thus, the cafeteria can make $\boxed{9}$ pies.  
